1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Large hotel near the beach in Pula, offering comfortable rooms, sports and wellness facilities, and easy access to both the coast and the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 3.4, "reviews": ["It’s hard to choose a hotel based on the reviews, as everyone has an expectation. This hotel is located near the beach, in the middle of a beautiful landscape. Offers parking, wi-fi, gym, swimming pool, breakfast and others. The quaro, though old, was clean and cozy. The service from the staff was excellent, as I had made a reservation that was cancelled and I was surprised at the time, but the boy, very kind, solved the problem. Thank you very much for your attention. The price was a little above the platform, but it was already a little late and we ended up staying there.", "This place really needs some love. Sure, lots of options for breakfast, but the visual aspect of spending time here leaves much to be desired. Ancient caprets in the halls tell stories. Not ones I would like to be part of.", "It's an old hotel that must have been great in its day. Now it's worn out but makes no pretensions about itself. It has got a nice looking pool but I didn't try it. The rooms are basic and the bathroom is best described as old but functional. Generally the hotel is clean and the staff friendly."]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
2. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
4. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Saluga", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "national_park", "sand", "paved", "playground", "island", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": null, "rating": 3.5, "reviews": ["A beautiful beach with a shower, a bench and a small park. It has an entrance to the sea for people with disabilities.", "A well-maintained beach for swimming, but not my type because it's concrete. There is shade and a bistro where you can eat and drink."]}}
5. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "sandwiches", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kukuriku", "phone": "+385 52 210 498", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 07:00-23:00; Fr-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su 07:30-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A relaxed city-center café, offering coffee, cocktails and casual sweet and savory snacks in a pleasant outdoor setting.", "reviews": ["Nice place, friendly waiter and really tasty food", "Loved this place! It has really good chocolate croissants and the cappuccino is also very good.", "Nice place in city center. A bit pricey. Aperol spritz 8eur, Hugo the same. Staff was nice and professional."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Ribarska Koliba", "phone": "+385 99 499 1306", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 13:00-20:00; Fr-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 13:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A refined seaside restaurant known for fresh local seafood, Mediterranean cuisine, Istrian wines, homemade desserts, and elegant dining with a sea view.", "reviews": ["A culinary highlight! The dishes are creative, refined and simply taste convincing. The service is friendly and attentive, the ambience warm and welcoming – perfect for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A little downer: The plates were cold, so the food quickly became lukewarm. Nevertheless, an all-round recommended visit!", "Exceptional food and service ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ Best lubina, stuffed swuid was excellent as well! Lovely setting for an evening meal.", "Nice view and good food! The only downside was that the main course came pretty soon after the starter. As a result, we were basically ready within an hour. We had to wait the longest for the bill 😅"], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "pizza", "pasta", "burgers", "salads", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Oliva", "phone": "+385 52 590 781", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant in the Verudela resort complex, set next to the pools and offering a varied menu of Istrian dishes, seafood, grilled meat, pizza, salads, pasta, burgers, and desserts in a relaxed holiday setting.", "reviews": ["This place is lovely. It’s sunny and right by the shore, with a beautiful sea view from inside. The service is friendly and fast - no long waiting times for food, which is a big plus. The Croatian dishes are delicious, the cocktails are great, and the prices are very reasonable. A perfect spot to relax, enjoy good food, and take in the view. Highly recommend!", "The location is just wonderful with great views and a feeling of space. We have eaten here now 3 times and each time the service has been good and the food excellent. The range of options available mean you should find something to your liking. Definitely recommended", "Oh my gosh never ever have I gotten the service this place offered me! Especially for a pool lounge! I asked if I could get some plastic cups for my water so I could drink it at the pool and they bring me the cups with ice 🧊 . It’s a kindness and this place is full of these little gestures! Amazing staff on a beautiful spot! Every visit was 5 stars!! Good cocktails ! Good food good icecream and a customer service focused on delivering the extra holiday feel!! I am a fan!"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
