1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Verudella", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "aquarium", "military_history", "family_friendly"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress on Punta Verudela, now home to Aquarium Pula and known for its military heritage and sea-facing setting.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Large hotel near the beach in Pula, offering comfortable rooms, sports and wellness facilities, and easy access to both the coast and the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 3.4, "reviews": ["It’s hard to choose a hotel based on the reviews, as everyone has an expectation. This hotel is located near the beach, in the middle of a beautiful landscape. Offers parking, wi-fi, gym, swimming pool, breakfast and others. The quaro, though old, was clean and cozy. The service from the staff was excellent, as I had made a reservation that was cancelled and I was surprised at the time, but the boy, very kind, solved the problem. Thank you very much for your attention. The price was a little above the platform, but it was already a little late and we ended up staying there.", "This place really needs some love. Sure, lots of options for breakfast, but the visual aspect of spending time here leaves much to be desired. Ancient caprets in the halls tell stories. Not ones I would like to be part of.", "It's an old hotel that must have been great in its day. Now it's worn out but makes no pretensions about itself. It has got a nice looking pool but I didn't try it. The rooms are basic and the bathroom is best described as old but functional. Generally the hotel is clean and the staff friendly."]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "gluten_free", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kažun", "phone": "+385 52 223 184", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Su 11:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "31", "addr:street": "Cesta Prekomorskih Brigada", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A rustic Istrian-style restaurant in a casual setting, offering traditional meat and fish dishes, homemade pasta, and local specialties, including its signature grilled steak.", "reviews": ["When I say this was the best meal of my life, I truly mean it! The food was absolutely delicious, and the service was outstanding. The steak in particular was incredible—I highly recommend it. This was by far one of the best dining experiences I’ve ever had. If you’re visiting Pula, you must come here. If you don’t, you’re seriously missing out!", "Charming restaurant with excellent seafood. We got the platter for two - guys really you have to try it. The chard was top here, fresh and tasty.", "Good food at the edge of Pula, friendly staff as well. Had a truffle pasta and a fresh cabbage (kupus) salad here, with real Istrian truffles. Delicious!"], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "pasta", "italian", "seafood", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pizzeria Tivoli", "phone": "+385 52 508 000", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 14:00-23:00; Fr-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Veli vrh", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A spacious pizzeria in Veli Vrh neighborhood, set within a sports complex and offering a wide variety of pizzas, pasta, salads, and family-friendly dining.", "reviews": ["Loved it! Delicious pizza and really good tiramisu. The staff was really nice as well. I was surprised how big this place is. Will come back for sure.", "Traveled a lot all around europe, tried gazzilion pasta and pizza places: this place has to be one of the BEST ever! Fine selection of pizza and pasta dishes. Quick service. Nice selection of additional olive oils and parmesan. My warmest recommendation.", "An excellent pizzeria, would definitely recommend. Great atmosphere - staff are friendly, incredibly busy, rushing around bringing food/drinks - service was impeccable and really well coordinated. There was a great variety of pizzas to choose from. We chose some of the local options, alongside some classics. A really popular place that is suitable for the whole family. There’s even a play area for the kids."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "pasta", "italian", "meat", "salads", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pizzeria LEMA", "phone": "+385 52 427 428", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "45", "addr:street": "Veruda", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual neighborhood pizzeria in Pula, best known for pizza delivery but also offering indoor and outdoor seating and a full menu for dine-in. The menu focuses on a wide range of classic and specialty pizzas, along with pasta, grilled meat dishes, salads, fish, and simple desserts, making it a convenient choice for both a quick meal and takeout.", "reviews": ["This place came recommended by our B&B host. We love a good spicy pizza do we ordered a Diavolo as a walk-in for carryout. The pizza was very good, but I wish they would cut the spicy peppers to help distribute them better. We did that ourselves which wasn't an issue. They have a nice little operation and can really churn out the pizza at a good pace. Everyone that was working genuinely seemed like they were having a good time. I think we maybe waited 15-20min. They also have a good selection of beers. I grabbed a couple of Leffe.", "If you're looking for a place to get pizza from in Pula then look no further because this is it. Great hard working and friendly staff, nice atmosphere and an amazing pizza. This is definitely a place that I'd visit every time I'm here in Pula. Absolutely great", "Very nice modern place. The pizza is made with excellent ingredients, baked in an old school fireplace, like it's suppose to be. You have three sizes of pizza available, small, medium and jumbo. The medium size is perfect for one hungry person. Jumbo is perfect for three people. I Highly recommend this excellent pizza place! :) The photo is of a medium (classic pizza size) and only 8euros, i was blown away!", "Excellent pizza, one medium pizza is enough for 2 adults. Also pasta carbonara was delicious."], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "pizza", "neapolitan_pizza", "beer", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Maximilian", "phone": "+385 52 496 938", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A modern pizzeria in Max City shopping center, known for authentic Neapolitan pizza with long-fermented dough and high-quality ingredients. With a spacious interior, large terrace, and a menu that includes both classic and gourmet pizzas, it is a popular spot for pizza lovers in Pula", "reviews": ["Very delicious pizza! Good choice of different pizzas and drinks. Service is very nice and friendly. Smiling and helping! Speaking English without any problems. Recommend to everyone! Delicious and good price 😊", "It's very nice. Not a particular ambient, being in a mall, it is quite a simple restaurant, but the pizza is great and interesting - some flavours we've never tried before. If you like very traditional pizza you might not be as interested, or take the capricciosa, but if you are up for experimenting with taste, take one of the Italian specialties - mortadela salami and pistachio pesto.", "Wonderful place to eat pizza! They also have gluten-free pizzas that are amazing! Really good in taste, the service was nice, and they were really fast. The staff was really nice too! I highly recommend this place! (I took the glue free pizza with mortadella that was really good ! )", "Amazing Pizza for a good price"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "italian", "pasta", "desserts", "grill", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pizzeria Diego", "phone": "+385 52 218 812", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 13:00-22:00; Su 13:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "23", "addr:street": "De Franceschijeva", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A casual pizzeria offering a wide variety of pizzas, along with pasta, desserts, and selected grill dishes.", "reviews": ["The former pizzeria Samantha in a new location with the same widely known pizzas. Excellent pizzas, cozy interior design and a great team that serves. The pizzas are big and delicious, the recommendation goes for their calzone and fantasia. Normal prices.", "What a great find. Short distance from the centre of Pula. I had a delicious truffle pasta which was a really generous portion for the price. The vegan pizza was also very good. Service is nice as well here.", "Best food for that price, no just pizzas. Excelent and friendly service. Good outdoor ambient for smokers. Very big problem with parking."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}

1. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Casoni Vecchi", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic circular hilltop fort in Pula, known for its Austro-Hungarian military heritage, panoramic views, and occasional cultural events.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["The Fort was built in 1852-1854 during the wars; currently stands empty and locked off to visitors. Nothing to see here, overgrown and rather dangerous.", "Beautiful structure that unfortunately is abandoned/locked from tourists. The Fort is hidden behind a big building and walls which hides its former beauty. It is in bad shape. Nothing to see here unfortunately."]}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Titov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "events", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central waterfront park in Pula, known for its memorial monuments, shaded walking areas, city model, and lively social atmosphere with seasonal events.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Tito's Park in Pula is a prominent public park that serves as a green oasis in the heart of the city. Named after Josip Broz Tito, the former Yugoslav leader, the park is a popular area for both locals and tourists seeking relaxation and recreation. There's also a miniature model on one side of the park.", "Nice park next to the water with many busts of famous partisans, including Tito. The main monument is also dedicated to the partisans. Worth a few pictures.", "A piece of more recent Croatian history. Has some statues, a place for kids to play, a few benches and a model of the city."]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
2. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Hostel Art & Joy", "tags": ["hostel", "free_parking", "garden", "family_friendly"], "description": "Friendly hostel in Pula with a garden, terrace, shared kitchen, and convenient access to the Arena and other city attractions.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["We had an amazing stay in this hostel. The staff is very nice and helpful : the receptionist gave us tips on what to see and visit around the city, helped us book bikes. We were also able to change beds to be closer to each other in the room. The bedrooms and common rooms are cleaned daily and the air conditioning was appreciated. The hostel is well located, there are bus stops right next to it, it’s only a 10-minutes walk to the city center. As 2 girls travelling, we felt very confortable and safe staying at this hostel. People we met there were easygoing and we had some really nice times in the kitchen and on the terrace. To sum up : we had a wonderful vacation in Pula :) PS : the only thing that’s missing would be board games accessible to everyone.", "We had a nice stay in the private room. Everything is clean, the staff is friendly, pizzeria next door. The cute mosaique and artistic flair got us lost in long conversations about art and the meaning of life ;)", "I have stayed in Pula 5 times now. The first time was at an apartment with restricted check in times. 3pm to 5pm only. And a long walk to the centre.I was in a restaurant chatting to someone on the next table.He recommended Art and Joy hostel. I took a walk there the next day. His advice was spot on. I met the manager there and said may I have a look inside, with a possibility of staying there the following year. She agreed. Wow it was great I thought. So I booked for the next Summer. I wasn't disappointed. I have now stayed 4 times each Summer for 4 years.Close to the centre, and the staff are superb. They will help you with any issues you may have.. The hard working cleaner is great also. I recommend it. Choice of rooms to suit your requirements.And good value.. Give it a try for a few nights and then extend it if you want to. Obviously subject to availability."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Amfiteatar", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "Boutique hotel in central Pula, just steps from the Arena, offering modern rooms, a well-known restaurant, and easy access to the old town and waterfront.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel, great location, very central. Lovely staff and extremely helpful with suggestions to eat and drink and booking a taxi to the airport. Room 101 was great, really spacious with bathrobes and slippers. Tea and coffee making facilities in the room. Great choice of both hot and cold food at breakfast. Would definitely stay again.", "I can’t get over what a great place this is! Location of course, front desk service, comfort, and value. I would highly recommend this facility for any type of visit to Pula.", "Great experience staying here! Location is superb and the staff is super friendly. We accidentally broke the tap in the bathroom while staying here, but the hotel staff just exchanged it during the day and it was fixed when we got back in the afternoon. Would definitely recommend staying here!"]}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
