5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Sergio Endrigo", "tags": ["park", "memorial", "near_attractions", "city_center"], "description": "Small urban park in central Pula dedicated to singer-songwriter Sergio Endrigo, with commemorative installations and occasional cultural events. Today it is mostly a quiet stop with a few benches and greenery, more suitable for a short pause than as a main attraction.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "pizza", "pasta", "burgers", "salads", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Oliva", "phone": "+385 52 590 781", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant in the Verudela resort complex, set next to the pools and offering a varied menu of Istrian dishes, seafood, grilled meat, pizza, salads, pasta, burgers, and desserts in a relaxed holiday setting.", "reviews": ["This place is lovely. It’s sunny and right by the shore, with a beautiful sea view from inside. The service is friendly and fast - no long waiting times for food, which is a big plus. The Croatian dishes are delicious, the cocktails are great, and the prices are very reasonable. A perfect spot to relax, enjoy good food, and take in the view. Highly recommend!", "The location is just wonderful with great views and a feeling of space. We have eaten here now 3 times and each time the service has been good and the food excellent. The range of options available mean you should find something to your liking. Definitely recommended", "Oh my gosh never ever have I gotten the service this place offered me! Especially for a pool lounge! I asked if I could get some plastic cups for my water so I could drink it at the pool and they bring me the cups with ice 🧊 . It’s a kindness and this place is full of these little gestures! Amazing staff on a beautiful spot! Every visit was 5 stars!! Good cocktails ! Good food good icecream and a customer service focused on delivering the extra holiday feel!! I am a fan!"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 52 634 385", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 08:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 3.4, "description": "A modern coffee bar and snack spot in Pula City Mall, offering quality coffee, fresh juices, sandwiches, cakes and sweet treats, ideal for a relaxed coffee break while shopping.", "reviews": ["Very expensive place to drink a coffe! Really too much! A price of a coffee in a supermarket must be more cheaper than one in the centre of the city…excessively!!!", "A very relaxing place whether you sit inside or outside on the terrace, with an excellent selection of food and drinks and outstanding, dedicated staff—especially the waiter Dylan, who is very fast, helpful, friendly, and fully committed to guests at all times, regardless of the crowd and high turnover of people!", "The coffee is average, but definitely not worth €2.90. I’ve had much better coffee for less money. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only one who thinks the quality doesn’t justify the price.", "Always smiling, helpful, and quick, even when dealing with guests who can be very rude and impatient. Kudos to them for their patience—they truly make an effort and give their best to do the job as well as possible. Highly recommended!"], "price": "high"}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "meat", "pasta", "burgers", "beer", "wine", "cocktails", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kinema", "phone": "+385 99 164 4949", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 10:00-23:00, Fr,Sa 10:00-24:00, Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Flavijevska", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A modern pub and restaurant in Pula with a lively social atmosphere, combining great food, drinks, and entertainment in one place. Kinema is known for billiards, darts, live sports screenings, themed events, burgers, steaks, breakfast, local wines, cocktails, and craft beer, making it a popular spot for both casual hangouts and nights out with friends.", "reviews": ["Fantastic bar/restaurant. Visiting from England I was looking for somewhere to watch the Aston Villa match, walked in I believe I met the owner, said he had the game on, minute later a guy came over and said you want the Villa game on the big screen, yes I said, that’s great hospitality! The bar is extremely cool, strangely it smells wonderful in there, darts, pool all can be played. Food is excellent, we had a grazing board and chicken wings, spot on they was. Staff, really friendly and welcoming, sorry about this as I couldn’t remember her name, but Drag….. was first class.", "One of the best restaurants in Pula, especially if you’re looking for a place to eat near the Pula Arena. The food portions were huge, definitely more than enough for one person, and we left feeling very full and satisfied. The drinks were excellent and had a classy touch. The ambiance was fantastic, with great entertainment and we didn’t even realize we had stayed for over 3 hours! Highly recommended.", "What a venue! If you are looking for live sports, pool, darts or just a good atmosphere, head here. An old cinema has been transformed into a superb sports bar. A small doorway opens up to this vast multi room venue, and the screen is maaaasssssiiiiiiiivvveee. A nice welcome to fast knowledgeable service & they go to every effort to accommodate your needs. After the large main room, there's a pool room off to one side & another more intimate balcony area upstairs. The atmosphere is not too loud, so you have to shout, and the other guests are all smiling and up to banter. The menu does not do justice to the food, which was excellent. A mix of burgers, etc, to more traditional dishes Generous portios, to say the least, could not even look at the desserts menu. A real gem * kids are welcome", "This was the best restaurant I've visited in Pula. Pavle, the server was extremely pleasant and welcoming, he gave some great suggestions. I came in only to have some coffee but ended up getting the breakfast and dessert. Couldn't tell which was better. Extremely well made food, with even better staff. I couldn't recommend this place more!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Baretini - Studio Lungomare", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking"], "description": "Modern and bright studio apartment in Pula, ideal for two guests, with a south-facing balcony, sea view, free parking, and a great location just a short walk from the beach and nearby beach bars.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "pancakes", "cakes", "sandwiches"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cookie", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": null, "description": "A modern café bar in Max City on Stoja with a spacious terrace, sea views, and a casual setting for coffee, desserts, and light meals.", "reviews": null, "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Saluga", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "national_park", "sand", "paved", "playground", "island", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": null, "rating": 3.5, "reviews": ["A beautiful beach with a shower, a bench and a small park. It has an entrance to the sea for people with disabilities.", "A well-maintained beach for swimming, but not my type because it's concrete. There is shade and a bistro where you can eat and drink."]}}

