1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 52 634 385", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 08:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 3.4, "description": "A modern coffee bar and snack spot in Pula City Mall, offering quality coffee, fresh juices, sandwiches, cakes and sweet treats, ideal for a relaxed coffee break while shopping.", "reviews": ["Very expensive place to drink a coffe! Really too much! A price of a coffee in a supermarket must be more cheaper than one in the centre of the city…excessively!!!", "A very relaxing place whether you sit inside or outside on the terrace, with an excellent selection of food and drinks and outstanding, dedicated staff—especially the waiter Dylan, who is very fast, helpful, friendly, and fully committed to guests at all times, regardless of the crowd and high turnover of people!", "The coffee is average, but definitely not worth €2.90. I’ve had much better coffee for less money. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only one who thinks the quality doesn’t justify the price.", "Always smiling, helpful, and quick, even when dealing with guests who can be very rude and impatient. Kudos to them for their patience—they truly make an effort and give their best to do the job as well as possible. Highly recommended!"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Giardino Bar", "phone": "+385 99 403 4680", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-24:00; Sa 07:00-01:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Giardini", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A cozy café in the center of Pula, ideal for coffee, ice cream, drinks, and a relaxing break.", "reviews": ["Nice place, great drink (teragino), the music wasn't loud, so it wasn't a problem to hear each other. And we got free chips and nuts with the drink.", "Great location and atmosphere and an extremely polite and helpful waiter, a real refreshment!", "Good music, delicious coffee, even a vegan milk option, and clean bathrooms."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Ribarska Koliba", "phone": "+385 99 499 1306", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 13:00-20:00; Fr-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 13:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A refined seaside restaurant known for fresh local seafood, Mediterranean cuisine, Istrian wines, homemade desserts, and elegant dining with a sea view.", "reviews": ["A culinary highlight! The dishes are creative, refined and simply taste convincing. The service is friendly and attentive, the ambience warm and welcoming – perfect for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A little downer: The plates were cold, so the food quickly became lukewarm. Nevertheless, an all-round recommended visit!", "Exceptional food and service ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ Best lubina, stuffed swuid was excellent as well! Lovely setting for an evening meal.", "Nice view and good food! The only downside was that the main course came pretty soon after the starter. As a result, we were basically ready within an hour. We had to wait the longest for the bill 😅"], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Kaiser Franz", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "island", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the island of Sveti Andrija in Pula, known for its circular form, layered military history, and strategic position in the middle of the harbour.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["Nice fort. It's a pity that it is neglected and completely overgrown. While sightseeing, it feels like walking through a jungle. There are a lot of snakes and rats. On the roof of the fortress there are a lot of hidden ventilation holes through which you can fall, so you need to be very careful."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Casoni Vecchi", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic circular hilltop fort in Pula, known for its Austro-Hungarian military heritage, panoramic views, and occasional cultural events.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["The Fort was built in 1852-1854 during the wars; currently stands empty and locked off to visitors. Nothing to see here, overgrown and rather dangerous.", "Beautiful structure that unfortunately is abandoned/locked from tourists. The Fort is hidden behind a big building and walls which hides its former beauty. It is in bad shape. Nothing to see here unfortunately."]}}
5. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "burgers", "fries", "seafood"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Big Mama Beachbar", "phone": "+385 95 581 0900", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Valovine", "rating": 3.5, "description": null, "reviews": ["Fantastic beach bar with a relaxed atmosphere and stunning sea views. The drinks are refreshing, the staff is friendly, and the music creates the perfect summer vibe. A great place to unwind and enjoy the sunset!", "The food is delicious and the staff is excellent! A beautiful place for a beach holiday. Beautiful sunset.", "We passed this bar on a walk along the coast. On the terrace you can sit very nicely and watch the wakeboarders who are active on the wakeboard system. We had Coke and non-alcoholic beer, each from a local vendor and well chilled. Cheeseburgers and classic burgers were well fried and delicious. The fries were great and the fried calamari crispy. Everything was served on a beautiful wooden board plastic-free. The young man who served us was very nice and spoke a very good English."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "wine", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Padela", "phone": "+385 91 6085 632", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Riva", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A stylish waterfront restaurant on Pula’s Riva, specializing in handmade pasta, risotto, seafood, wine, and seasonal local ingredients.", "reviews": ["Excellent experience dining at this unique and wonderful restaurant! Beautifully decorated and very kind, professional service. We immediately felt welcomed. The waiter was also very helpful with describing the different dishes and house made pastas. Highly recommended.", "Fine dining with local touch and amazing ingredients. We were super amazed about the quality and taste of food. The pasta is perfectly cooked with carefully combined flavors and sauce. Thanks to the chef and team for the experience! 👏", "Padela is wonderful small restaurant with such a sweet atmosphere. Our server was so lovely and gave us exceptional wine recommendations. The pasta is to die for and the seafood is clearly very fresh. Highly recommend adding this place to your time in Pula!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
2. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "pizza", "pasta", "burgers", "salads", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Oliva", "phone": "+385 52 590 781", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant in the Verudela resort complex, set next to the pools and offering a varied menu of Istrian dishes, seafood, grilled meat, pizza, salads, pasta, burgers, and desserts in a relaxed holiday setting.", "reviews": ["This place is lovely. It’s sunny and right by the shore, with a beautiful sea view from inside. The service is friendly and fast - no long waiting times for food, which is a big plus. The Croatian dishes are delicious, the cocktails are great, and the prices are very reasonable. A perfect spot to relax, enjoy good food, and take in the view. Highly recommend!", "The location is just wonderful with great views and a feeling of space. We have eaten here now 3 times and each time the service has been good and the food excellent. The range of options available mean you should find something to your liking. Definitely recommended", "Oh my gosh never ever have I gotten the service this place offered me! Especially for a pool lounge! I asked if I could get some plastic cups for my water so I could drink it at the pool and they bring me the cups with ice 🧊 . It’s a kindness and this place is full of these little gestures! Amazing staff on a beautiful spot! Every visit was 5 stars!! Good cocktails ! Good food good icecream and a customer service focused on delivering the extra holiday feel!! I am a fan!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Scala", "phone": "+385 98 898 484", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Ozad Arene", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A simple café bar right next to the Pula Arena, best known for its unique terrace with a direct view of the amphitheatre. It is a relaxed spot for coffee or a drink in one of the city’s most iconic locations.", "reviews": ["Perfect place to watch the Arena and enjoy a cold drink! Personnel is nice and friendly. Prices are regular. Have you never visited Croatia before? Try Pasareta, a real Croatian drink! 💪🏼 with lots of ice cubes, perfect! We only had drinks, no food. They have a lot of ice creams!", "Great coffee bar / drinks. Best spot in the area for a quiet coffee and to enjoy the arena. The staff all spoke many languages and were very helpful on giving local recommendations.", "Service extremely friendly and attentive. Nice ambience (with music from the amphitheater). Just perfect, where you feel comfortable and enjoy the sunset. Can only recommend👌"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Casoni Vecchi", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic circular hilltop fort in Pula, known for its Austro-Hungarian military heritage, panoramic views, and occasional cultural events.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["The Fort was built in 1852-1854 during the wars; currently stands empty and locked off to visitors. Nothing to see here, overgrown and rather dangerous.", "Beautiful structure that unfortunately is abandoned/locked from tourists. The Fort is hidden behind a big building and walls which hides its former beauty. It is in bad shape. Nothing to see here unfortunately."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda San Michele", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area", "city_center"], "description": "Historic horseshoe-shaped fortress on the San Michele hill in Pula, built as part of the city’s defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and long later use within the hospital complex.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["One of many fortresses located in Pula, and I would say one of my favorites, sadly no one maintains them and they are falling apart. This is beautiful city with rich history and so many potetial and 0 will to restore them... who knows, maybe one day the people who manage the city will get into their heads that Pula is not only the sea and the Arena... Pula is much more...", "It could be an attraction if it wasn't completely neglected."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 52 634 385", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 08:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 3.4, "description": "A modern coffee bar and snack spot in Pula City Mall, offering quality coffee, fresh juices, sandwiches, cakes and sweet treats, ideal for a relaxed coffee break while shopping.", "reviews": ["Very expensive place to drink a coffe! Really too much! A price of a coffee in a supermarket must be more cheaper than one in the centre of the city…excessively!!!", "A very relaxing place whether you sit inside or outside on the terrace, with an excellent selection of food and drinks and outstanding, dedicated staff—especially the waiter Dylan, who is very fast, helpful, friendly, and fully committed to guests at all times, regardless of the crowd and high turnover of people!", "The coffee is average, but definitely not worth €2.90. I’ve had much better coffee for less money. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only one who thinks the quality doesn’t justify the price.", "Always smiling, helpful, and quick, even when dealing with guests who can be very rude and impatient. Kudos to them for their patience—they truly make an effort and give their best to do the job as well as possible. Highly recommended!"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Giardino Bar", "phone": "+385 99 403 4680", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-24:00; Sa 07:00-01:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Giardini", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A cozy café in the center of Pula, ideal for coffee, ice cream, drinks, and a relaxing break.", "reviews": ["Nice place, great drink (teragino), the music wasn't loud, so it wasn't a problem to hear each other. And we got free chips and nuts with the drink.", "Great location and atmosphere and an extremely polite and helpful waiter, a real refreshment!", "Good music, delicious coffee, even a vegan milk option, and clean bathrooms."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Golub mira", "tags": ["artwork", "sculpture", "memorial", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A symbolic outdoor sculpture created by Dušan Džamonja and donated to the Brijuni archipelago in memory of Josip Broz Tito. Made of corten and formed from welded iron chains, it was conceived as a powerful expression of peace and freedom, combining modern artistic form with historical remembrance.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["bakery", "breakfast", "coffee", "pizza", "sandwiches", "desserts", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mlinar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-20:00; Sa 06:30-15:00; Su 07:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A casual Mlinar cafe next to the city market, offering baked goods, pastries, sandwiches, and self-service coffee in a simple indoor seating area. It is a convenient spot for a quick breakfast, snack, or coffee break in the city center.", "reviews": ["Everything I've gotten to eat at any Mlinar has been delicious and a good price. I usually avoid chains, but they're just so good!", "Unfortunately the coffee is produced by an automatic machine... So nothing really special The food is okeish, I cannot complain. If you are hungry and you cannot find anything else around, this place will be fine.", "Good bakery, but coffe is overpriced (2 eur for coffe in paper cup?). 🙄Price of yoghurt is also quite high (1.8 eur) - I remember the times then normal price was 0.4 eur (few years ago). 🤑 I had a chicken burek here and I was suprised that I liked it more than traditional one ( with beef )"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Saluga", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "national_park", "sand", "paved", "playground", "island", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": null, "rating": 3.5, "reviews": ["A beautiful beach with a shower, a bench and a small park. It has an entrance to the sea for people with disabilities.", "A well-maintained beach for swimming, but not my type because it's concrete. There is shade and a bistro where you can eat and drink."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
5. {"type": "ruins", "properties": {"name": "ruševine Hidrobaze", "tags": ["ruins", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Former military ruin in the Hidrobaza area near Štinjan, currently in a neglected state and notable for its abandoned structure, graffiti, and position near the beach and promenade.", "rating": 3.9, "reviews": ["Interesting ruins (of an old seaplane base if I got it right) close to the beach. As usual in lost places close civilisation a lot of waste, racial slurs graffitied, and broken glass. Still quite interesting to see, but maybe don't bring your kids, don't go alone (floor partially collapsed), and watch your steps.", "I don't know who owns it at the moment, but it's an important memento of Hungarian history: a seaplane base headquarters. It's a shame.", "It's a shame these ruins have been left to decay. A wonderful 'lost place.'"]}}

1. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Sergio Endrigo", "tags": ["park", "memorial", "near_attractions", "city_center"], "description": "Small urban park in central Pula dedicated to singer-songwriter Sergio Endrigo, with commemorative installations and occasional cultural events. Today it is mostly a quiet stop with a few benches and greenery, more suitable for a short pause than as a main attraction.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}

1. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda San Michele", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area", "city_center"], "description": "Historic horseshoe-shaped fortress on the San Michele hill in Pula, built as part of the city’s defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and long later use within the hospital complex.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["One of many fortresses located in Pula, and I would say one of my favorites, sadly no one maintains them and they are falling apart. This is beautiful city with rich history and so many potetial and 0 will to restore them... who knows, maybe one day the people who manage the city will get into their heads that Pula is not only the sea and the Arena... Pula is much more...", "It could be an attraction if it wasn't completely neglected."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Stoja", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and strategic position above the southern approach to the harbour.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very beautiful places with the opportunity to jump from cliffs.", "I unexpectedly discovered this place, a mound. Fort Stoja is one of the most mysterious and 'hidden' forts in Pula. Built in 1884 by the Austro-Hungarians as part of a powerful coastal defense for the empire's main naval base. Unlike most forts, Stoja is almost completely dug into the peninsula's limestone cliff: only a massive entrance wall with a portal is visible from the outside, while the rest is hidden underground and covered by a dense pine forest. It is surrounded by a deep moat cut into the rock, once filled with water and protected by caponiers. On three sides, the fort plunges directly into the sea, making it virtually invisible from the water or from the air. Inside are long casemates, powder magazines, and posterns extending into the hillside. After the First World War, it lost its military significance and gradually became overgrown with forest, becoming a 'ghost fort.' Today the moat is dry, but the walls and entrance are impressive: it seems as if the mountain itself opens a huge door to the 19th century. An ideal place for those who enjoy the atmosphere of abandoned fortifications, peace and quiet, and views of the Adriatic without the crowds of tourists.", "Beautiful campsite, convenient for Pula by bus. The fort is not accessible and is at the top of the peninsula."]}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "meat", "pasta", "burgers", "beer", "wine", "cocktails", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kinema", "phone": "+385 99 164 4949", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 10:00-23:00, Fr,Sa 10:00-24:00, Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Flavijevska", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A modern pub and restaurant in Pula with a lively social atmosphere, combining great food, drinks, and entertainment in one place. Kinema is known for billiards, darts, live sports screenings, themed events, burgers, steaks, breakfast, local wines, cocktails, and craft beer, making it a popular spot for both casual hangouts and nights out with friends.", "reviews": ["Fantastic bar/restaurant. Visiting from England I was looking for somewhere to watch the Aston Villa match, walked in I believe I met the owner, said he had the game on, minute later a guy came over and said you want the Villa game on the big screen, yes I said, that’s great hospitality! The bar is extremely cool, strangely it smells wonderful in there, darts, pool all can be played. Food is excellent, we had a grazing board and chicken wings, spot on they was. Staff, really friendly and welcoming, sorry about this as I couldn’t remember her name, but Drag….. was first class.", "One of the best restaurants in Pula, especially if you’re looking for a place to eat near the Pula Arena. The food portions were huge, definitely more than enough for one person, and we left feeling very full and satisfied. The drinks were excellent and had a classy touch. The ambiance was fantastic, with great entertainment and we didn’t even realize we had stayed for over 3 hours! Highly recommended.", "What a venue! If you are looking for live sports, pool, darts or just a good atmosphere, head here. An old cinema has been transformed into a superb sports bar. A small doorway opens up to this vast multi room venue, and the screen is maaaasssssiiiiiiiivvveee. A nice welcome to fast knowledgeable service & they go to every effort to accommodate your needs. After the large main room, there's a pool room off to one side & another more intimate balcony area upstairs. The atmosphere is not too loud, so you have to shout, and the other guests are all smiling and up to banter. The menu does not do justice to the food, which was excellent. A mix of burgers, etc, to more traditional dishes Generous portios, to say the least, could not even look at the desserts menu. A real gem * kids are welcome", "This was the best restaurant I've visited in Pula. Pavle, the server was extremely pleasant and welcoming, he gave some great suggestions. I came in only to have some coffee but ended up getting the breakfast and dessert. Couldn't tell which was better. Extremely well made food, with even better staff. I couldn't recommend this place more!"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "coffee", "gallery", "cocktails", "ice_cream", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cvajner", "phone": "+385 52 216 502", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-23:00; Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.3, "description": "Art café and gallery on Pula’s main square, known for its striking historic interior, artistic atmosphere, and terrace overlooking the Forum and the Temple of Augustus.", "reviews": ["Great place to get some coffee and quick food; located right in Forum Square, so finding this place is super simple. Service could be a bit better and more organized, but otherwise everything was super tasty.", "Very nice iced coffee. Cozy enviroment, interesting design with restored paintings on the walls.", "This is in a great location if you sit outside. The Forum has a great buzz and is beautiful. Prices are quite reasonable for such a location (big draught beer €4.2) Most of the staff are busy and seem a bit a bit grumpy ( except one nice waitress) There are small menus on the tables and bills are clearly itemised. We saw a family leave after waiting ages to be served. Inside looks nice too with some old frescos. Locals here too. Worth a visit though.", "Gorgeous and cosy caffe... Well preserved historical charm done by keeping the original tapestry and blending it in with the new one. Drinks are well made and the staff is polite, very nice place to come to on a rainy day."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Golub mira", "tags": ["artwork", "sculpture", "memorial", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A symbolic outdoor sculpture created by Dušan Džamonja and donated to the Brijuni archipelago in memory of Josip Broz Tito. Made of corten and formed from welded iron chains, it was conceived as a powerful expression of peace and freedom, combining modern artistic form with historical remembrance.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["bakery", "breakfast", "coffee", "pizza", "sandwiches", "desserts", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mlinar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-20:00; Sa 06:30-15:00; Su 07:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A casual Mlinar cafe next to the city market, offering baked goods, pastries, sandwiches, and self-service coffee in a simple indoor seating area. It is a convenient spot for a quick breakfast, snack, or coffee break in the city center.", "reviews": ["Everything I've gotten to eat at any Mlinar has been delicious and a good price. I usually avoid chains, but they're just so good!", "Unfortunately the coffee is produced by an automatic machine... So nothing really special The food is okeish, I cannot complain. If you are hungry and you cannot find anything else around, this place will be fine.", "Good bakery, but coffe is overpriced (2 eur for coffe in paper cup?). 🙄Price of yoghurt is also quite high (1.8 eur) - I remember the times then normal price was 0.4 eur (few years ago). 🤑 I had a chicken burek here and I was suprised that I liked it more than traditional one ( with beef )"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Monte Munide", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Small 19th-century circular artillery tower above Štinjan, surrounded by forest and known for its military history and quiet hilltop setting.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. The remains of it to be exact as it was bombarded in WW II and never reconstructed or conserved since. There is a worn-out info panel and a narrow path to the inside of the fort which is overgrown in trees and bush. There is nothing special to see, only to witness the utmost negligence and incompetence of the locals towards their own legacy. Dissapointing.", "Nice example of historical forts unfortunately blown up durning ww2", "Whole hill is full of military tunnels and bunkers. At the top is historycal Austrohungarian 19. century fort, 50 meters away is entrance to Yugoslavian era bunker, and right bellow the hill towards sea is another large bunker"]}}
4. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Paula von Preradović", "tags": ["plaque", "memorial", "historic"], "description": "Memorial plaque dedicated to Paula von Preradović, poet and author of the lyrics of the Austrian national anthem, marking the house near Pula’s Naval Park where she spent part of her childhood and youth. The plaque commemorates her literary legacy and her lasting connection to Pula.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Memorial plaque for the poet of the Austrian national anthem, who also wrote poems about Pula and lived here for some time."]}}
5. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Žena s mijehom", "tags": ["artwork", "sculpture", "island", "national_park", "monument"], "description": "Žena s mijehom is a bronze sculpture by Frane Kršinić, created in 1956 and located in Brijuni National Park as part of the Živa voda memorial site. The sculpture depicts a woman bending forward and pouring water from a goatskin bag into a stone basin below, symbolizing the importance of fresh water on the island. It is both an artistic landmark and a memorial to the technical achievement of discovering and drawing underground spring water on Brijuni.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Ovine", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal"], "description": "Abandoned Austro-Hungarian coastal fort in the Valovine area, known for its atmospheric tunnels, overgrown walls, and striking rooftop views over the sea.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["It was a small ruin with an entrance, a hallway, some rooms and a tunnel to a small katacomb. The dark tunnel which looks like the entrance of a katacomb has a slight slope and is slippery. Unfortunately some of the rooms were used as toilets - no understanding for that... The parking lots are kind off in front of fort and very busy. So make shure to plan your visit in the morning.", "Nothing special about this place, I have only visited the exterior though. I don't know if I suggest the visit. There is a civil guard near the entrance", "A fortification overgrown in the rock. Large areas are empty and dark. For those who enjoy extreme sports, this is for you."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Verudella", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "aquarium", "military_history", "family_friendly"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress on Punta Verudela, now home to Aquarium Pula and known for its military heritage and sea-facing setting.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Kaiser Franz", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "island", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the island of Sveti Andrija in Pula, known for its circular form, layered military history, and strategic position in the middle of the harbour.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["Nice fort. It's a pity that it is neglected and completely overgrown. While sightseeing, it feels like walking through a jungle. There are a lot of snakes and rats. On the roof of the fortress there are a lot of hidden ventilation holes through which you can fall, so you need to be very careful."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "steak", "pasta", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Veritas Food & Wine", "phone": "+385 97 656 3627", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "14", "addr:street": "Maksimijanova", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A family-run restaurant in the heart of Pula, known for seafood, steaks, pasta, Istrian wines, and a romantic atmosphere beside historic landmarks.", "reviews": ["We were having an amazing experience. Tonight we try all the productes with truffles. Pasta with truffles, steak with truffles and fish fillet with truffles, they even have beer with truffles!! For start we had 2 Hibiki Japanese whiskeys, and later with the food we shared a bottle of Matosevic Grimalda.", "Some of the best fishing scampi I've had. Already had high expectations with the great reviews but this blew me away. Definitely coming back on our next visit.", "Walking by I thought this restaurant was super cute and then looking at the menu, my husband and I walked back to go. We are so thankful we did! The food was amazing. The service was impeccable. They paired the drinks perfectly, recommended the freshest and best dishes, and even gave you the option to clean the fish themselves at the table. Very personable and friendly staff who work as a team but gave you the space to enjoy your time. The view and breeze was an added bonus. If I could give more stars, I absolutely would. Adding to my files of recommended eateries to share with family and friends who travel to Pula!", "We just had dinner here and it was above and beyond what we were expecting. We had a few dinners in Pula that were just okay but this was amazing. Arian gave excellent service while handling a huge section and a wait. We tried the scallops and local cheese for an appetizer. The scallops were perfectly prepared and the cheese was all local. Now for the main dishes. My better half had the lamb. Completely drool worthy, while I on the other hand had the truffle steak with the hand made pasta. Look no further! This was the best steak I have ever had. If we lived here we would come every week. The biggest issue is now I feel like I need truffles in every thing!"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "meat", "wine", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kantina", "phone": "+385 52 214 054", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "16", "addr:street": "Flanatička", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Classic Mediterranean eatery with stone walls & a terrace serving seafood, meat dishes & wine.", "reviews": ["Excellent food, friendly and prompt staff. Highly recommand. It is also 8 minutes walk from The Arena and 5 minutes from the beautiful center.", "Impeccable Service (they speak Italian), the place is quiet and out of the confusion, we were offered an appetizer with cheese and truffles which was delicious, then we had salmon and white fish and they were really exceptional. Great value for money. We arrived on foot walking through the center but if you want there is also a convenient parking. Highly recommended!", "Kantina Restaurant was a very beautiful surprise! We found the restaurant based on other very good reviews and we were more than satisfied. The restaurant is located a few hundred meters from Paula's center, and is very easy to reach. We had a full meal based on truffle dishes that were delicious. The waiter was extremely professional and kind and, in addition to our order, we have received a starter and a small amaro at the end of the dinner. Highly recommend!", "Dining at Restaurant Kantina in Pula was an absolute delight from start to finish. The whole fish I ordered was nothing short of spectacular—fresh, perfectly cooked, and bursting with authentic Mediterranean flavors that truly showcased the quality of local seafood. What made the experience even more memorable was the impeccable service. The staff delivered a level of fine dining hospitality that felt both professional and warmly personal."], "price": "high"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "neapolitan_pizza", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "pasta", "beer", "vegetarian", "gluten_free", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fabbrica", "phone": "385 52 894 6249", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "35", "addr:street": "Kandlerova", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A modern restaurant in old town, set in a renovated former boiler house with a distinctive industrial atmosphere. Fabbrica is known for Neapolitan pizza, BBQ dishes, burgers, craft beer, and a creative menu that blends authentic Italian flavors with local Istrian ingredients.", "reviews": ["A perfect place for a dinner with friends after a day at the beach! After a little walk from the Arena trough a busy central area on a summer Friday evening we stopped at this unique restaurant. We got a big table at the corner inside nearby the garden. The ventilation, the lights, the overall design with attention to details like beauty of natural field flowers in big vases and vintage style glasses. I have ordered the fish plate which contained of 3 differently graduated seafood, from sweet&sour marinated sepia to salty anchovies. A glass of sparkling wine married perfectly this gastronomic experience. It was something different from what I could ate in other restaurants at the coast. Compliments to the waiters service, so attentive yet discret. Highly recommended!", "Only popped in for a beer but a stunning eatery. Huge selection of beers. Very clean and service was excellent.", "Lovely local craft beers, spanning from Zagreb to Istria. The ambiance of their back garden is incredible, with views of a beautiful tree, fresh herbs, and freshly cut logs for the wood fire pizza oven. Highly recommend this restaurant for great service and a chill vibe. It’s also dog friendly!"], "price": "high"}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}

1. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "meat", "pasta", "burgers", "beer", "wine", "cocktails", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kinema", "phone": "+385 99 164 4949", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 10:00-23:00, Fr,Sa 10:00-24:00, Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Flavijevska", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A modern pub and restaurant in Pula with a lively social atmosphere, combining great food, drinks, and entertainment in one place. Kinema is known for billiards, darts, live sports screenings, themed events, burgers, steaks, breakfast, local wines, cocktails, and craft beer, making it a popular spot for both casual hangouts and nights out with friends.", "reviews": ["Fantastic bar/restaurant. Visiting from England I was looking for somewhere to watch the Aston Villa match, walked in I believe I met the owner, said he had the game on, minute later a guy came over and said you want the Villa game on the big screen, yes I said, that’s great hospitality! The bar is extremely cool, strangely it smells wonderful in there, darts, pool all can be played. Food is excellent, we had a grazing board and chicken wings, spot on they was. Staff, really friendly and welcoming, sorry about this as I couldn’t remember her name, but Drag….. was first class.", "One of the best restaurants in Pula, especially if you’re looking for a place to eat near the Pula Arena. The food portions were huge, definitely more than enough for one person, and we left feeling very full and satisfied. The drinks were excellent and had a classy touch. The ambiance was fantastic, with great entertainment and we didn’t even realize we had stayed for over 3 hours! Highly recommended.", "What a venue! If you are looking for live sports, pool, darts or just a good atmosphere, head here. An old cinema has been transformed into a superb sports bar. A small doorway opens up to this vast multi room venue, and the screen is maaaasssssiiiiiiiivvveee. A nice welcome to fast knowledgeable service & they go to every effort to accommodate your needs. After the large main room, there's a pool room off to one side & another more intimate balcony area upstairs. The atmosphere is not too loud, so you have to shout, and the other guests are all smiling and up to banter. The menu does not do justice to the food, which was excellent. A mix of burgers, etc, to more traditional dishes Generous portios, to say the least, could not even look at the desserts menu. A real gem * kids are welcome", "This was the best restaurant I've visited in Pula. Pavle, the server was extremely pleasant and welcoming, he gave some great suggestions. I came in only to have some coffee but ended up getting the breakfast and dessert. Couldn't tell which was better. Extremely well made food, with even better staff. I couldn't recommend this place more!"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "pasta", "seafood", "desserts", "italian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Pomodoro", "phone": "+385 52 218 093", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 10:00-23:00; Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Ulica Sergijevaca", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A casual restaurant in the heart of Pula’s old town, located on one of the main central streets and serving pizza, pasta, seafood, and desserts in a lively setting.", "reviews": ["Surprisingly best restaurant we visited here. Everyday we tried some different restaurant, everything was good but this one was so good that I decided to write this review :) Waitress was very polite and helpful. Taste of food was just outstanding. This was very good experience wort every penny. We all agreed that we had to come back here. Thank you Pomodoro", "Very good pizza and tagliatelle. Waitress was very nice and helpful when we asked questions about some meals. Be careful not to order too much! Size of the meal is rather big.", "An absolutely perfect experience at Restaurant Pomodoro in Pula! 🌟 From the moment we sat down, everything was flawless – exceptional service, professional and friendly waiters who made us feel welcome right away. 🍷 The food was simply outstanding! The pizzas were a highlight – Tartufo and Quattro Formaggi were absolutely amazing, with a perfect dough that was light yet crispy in just the right way. The fish was beautifully prepared, fresh and full of flavor, a true Mediterranean delight. The white wines were perfectly chilled and paired wonderfully with the meal. 🐟🍕 Restaurant Pomodoro deserves every recommendation – a must-visit spot for a true gourmet experience in Pula! 👌✨"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Titov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "events", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central waterfront park in Pula, known for its memorial monuments, shaded walking areas, city model, and lively social atmosphere with seasonal events.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Tito's Park in Pula is a prominent public park that serves as a green oasis in the heart of the city. Named after Josip Broz Tito, the former Yugoslav leader, the park is a popular area for both locals and tourists seeking relaxation and recreation. There's also a miniature model on one side of the park.", "Nice park next to the water with many busts of famous partisans, including Tito. The main monument is also dedicated to the partisans. Worth a few pictures.", "A piece of more recent Croatian history. Has some statues, a place for kids to play, a few benches and a model of the city."]}}
4. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
5. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Large hotel near the beach in Pula, offering comfortable rooms, sports and wellness facilities, and easy access to both the coast and the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 3.4, "reviews": ["It’s hard to choose a hotel based on the reviews, as everyone has an expectation. This hotel is located near the beach, in the middle of a beautiful landscape. Offers parking, wi-fi, gym, swimming pool, breakfast and others. The quaro, though old, was clean and cozy. The service from the staff was excellent, as I had made a reservation that was cancelled and I was surprised at the time, but the boy, very kind, solved the problem. Thank you very much for your attention. The price was a little above the platform, but it was already a little late and we ended up staying there.", "This place really needs some love. Sure, lots of options for breakfast, but the visual aspect of spending time here leaves much to be desired. Ancient caprets in the halls tell stories. Not ones I would like to be part of.", "It's an old hotel that must have been great in its day. Now it's worn out but makes no pretensions about itself. It has got a nice looking pool but I didn't try it. The rooms are basic and the bathroom is best described as old but functional. Generally the hotel is clean and the staff friendly."]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["bakery", "breakfast", "coffee", "pizza", "sandwiches", "desserts", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mlinar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-20:00; Sa 06:30-15:00; Su 07:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A casual Mlinar cafe next to the city market, offering baked goods, pastries, sandwiches, and self-service coffee in a simple indoor seating area. It is a convenient spot for a quick breakfast, snack, or coffee break in the city center.", "reviews": ["Everything I've gotten to eat at any Mlinar has been delicious and a good price. I usually avoid chains, but they're just so good!", "Unfortunately the coffee is produced by an automatic machine... So nothing really special The food is okeish, I cannot complain. If you are hungry and you cannot find anything else around, this place will be fine.", "Good bakery, but coffe is overpriced (2 eur for coffe in paper cup?). 🙄Price of yoghurt is also quite high (1.8 eur) - I remember the times then normal price was 0.4 eur (few years ago). 🤑 I had a chicken burek here and I was suprised that I liked it more than traditional one ( with beef )"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "mediterranean", "coffee", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Diana", "phone": "+385 98 915 4270", "opening_hours": "Mo-We 08:00-01:00; Th 08:00-24:00; Fr 08:00-01:00; Sa 08:00-24:00; Su 08:00-23:30", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Café on Pula’s Forum square with a large terrace, classic coffee-and-drinks offer, and a prime spot for sitting right in the heart of the old town.", "reviews": ["Nice café in the center of Pula. Basic coffee options but good quality and reasonably priced. Pleasant spot for a quick break.", "Nice little café with reasonable prices. Their ice coffee tastes nice.", "I highly recommend this bar, service was extremly fast and our waitress was very kind. Great location and great drinks. I’ll definitely return."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "burgers", "fries", "seafood"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Big Mama Beachbar", "phone": "+385 95 581 0900", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Valovine", "rating": 3.5, "description": null, "reviews": ["Fantastic beach bar with a relaxed atmosphere and stunning sea views. The drinks are refreshing, the staff is friendly, and the music creates the perfect summer vibe. A great place to unwind and enjoy the sunset!", "The food is delicious and the staff is excellent! A beautiful place for a beach holiday. Beautiful sunset.", "We passed this bar on a walk along the coast. On the terrace you can sit very nicely and watch the wakeboarders who are active on the wakeboard system. We had Coke and non-alcoholic beer, each from a local vendor and well chilled. Cheeseburgers and classic burgers were well fried and delicious. The fries were great and the fried calamari crispy. Everything was served on a beautiful wooden board plastic-free. The young man who served us was very nice and spoke a very good English."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "wine", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Padela", "phone": "+385 91 6085 632", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Riva", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A stylish waterfront restaurant on Pula’s Riva, specializing in handmade pasta, risotto, seafood, wine, and seasonal local ingredients.", "reviews": ["Excellent experience dining at this unique and wonderful restaurant! Beautifully decorated and very kind, professional service. We immediately felt welcomed. The waiter was also very helpful with describing the different dishes and house made pastas. Highly recommended.", "Fine dining with local touch and amazing ingredients. We were super amazed about the quality and taste of food. The pasta is perfectly cooked with carefully combined flavors and sauce. Thanks to the chef and team for the experience! 👏", "Padela is wonderful small restaurant with such a sweet atmosphere. Our server was so lovely and gave us exceptional wine recommendations. The pasta is to die for and the seafood is clearly very fresh. Highly recommend adding this place to your time in Pula!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "wine", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sirena", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-24:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed café on Pula’s main square, offering coffee, wine, cocktails, and terrace seating with views of the historic Forum.", "reviews": ["Wonderful place for coffee or a glass of delicious wine, with a view of the beautiful buildings around Forum Square. During our visits, we had the pleasure to meet waitress with long, slightly wavy hair — she was sooo cool and perfectly handled all orders. We'd love to come back! ❤️", "Nice terrace on the square! During the day, lots of shadow because of the wide parasols! The square is open, don’t get sunburned !", "Nice place, amazing coctails and lovely staff!"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Verudella", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "aquarium", "military_history", "family_friendly"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress on Punta Verudela, now home to Aquarium Pula and known for its military heritage and sea-facing setting.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
2. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Hostel Art & Joy", "tags": ["hostel", "free_parking", "garden", "family_friendly"], "description": "Friendly hostel in Pula with a garden, terrace, shared kitchen, and convenient access to the Arena and other city attractions.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["We had an amazing stay in this hostel. The staff is very nice and helpful : the receptionist gave us tips on what to see and visit around the city, helped us book bikes. We were also able to change beds to be closer to each other in the room. The bedrooms and common rooms are cleaned daily and the air conditioning was appreciated. The hostel is well located, there are bus stops right next to it, it’s only a 10-minutes walk to the city center. As 2 girls travelling, we felt very confortable and safe staying at this hostel. People we met there were easygoing and we had some really nice times in the kitchen and on the terrace. To sum up : we had a wonderful vacation in Pula :) PS : the only thing that’s missing would be board games accessible to everyone.", "We had a nice stay in the private room. Everything is clean, the staff is friendly, pizzeria next door. The cute mosaique and artistic flair got us lost in long conversations about art and the meaning of life ;)", "I have stayed in Pula 5 times now. The first time was at an apartment with restricted check in times. 3pm to 5pm only. And a long walk to the centre.I was in a restaurant chatting to someone on the next table.He recommended Art and Joy hostel. I took a walk there the next day. His advice was spot on. I met the manager there and said may I have a look inside, with a possibility of staying there the following year. She agreed. Wow it was great I thought. So I booked for the next Summer. I wasn't disappointed. I have now stayed 4 times each Summer for 4 years.Close to the centre, and the staff are superb. They will help you with any issues you may have.. The hard working cleaner is great also. I recommend it. Choice of rooms to suit your requirements.And good value.. Give it a try for a few nights and then extend it if you want to. Obviously subject to availability."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Amfiteatar", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "Boutique hotel in central Pula, just steps from the Arena, offering modern rooms, a well-known restaurant, and easy access to the old town and waterfront.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel, great location, very central. Lovely staff and extremely helpful with suggestions to eat and drink and booking a taxi to the airport. Room 101 was great, really spacious with bathrobes and slippers. Tea and coffee making facilities in the room. Great choice of both hot and cold food at breakfast. Would definitely stay again.", "I can’t get over what a great place this is! Location of course, front desk service, comfort, and value. I would highly recommend this facility for any type of visit to Pula.", "Great experience staying here! Location is superb and the staff is super friendly. We accidentally broke the tap in the bathroom while staying here, but the hotel staff just exchanged it during the day and it was fixed when we got back in the afternoon. Would definitely recommend staying here!"]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
5. {"type": "fountain", "properties": {"name": "Maketa Pule", "tags": ["tactile_model", "city_center", "interactive", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Interactive tactile model of Pula in the city centre, offering a detailed 3D overview of the city layout, waterways, and key landmarks in a quick and educational way.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["I love seeing the miniature cities; and this one is even cooler because it has water spouting where the Adriatic Sea is; really neat.", "Small model of the city of Pula, with water. Good for exploring the city. Made of metal.", "A visual miniature of the charming city of Pula. It's a great introduction to general knowledge. I highly recommend it."]}}

1. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "healthy", "brunch", "breakfast", "international", "vegan", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kavana Lattiera", "phone": "+385 91 537 4711", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00; Sa-Su 09:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Trg Kralja Tomislava", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A modern cafe in Veruda known for specialty coffee, healthy breakfasts, smoothie bowls, homemade cakes, and a relaxed neighborhood atmosphere. Inspired by Berlin-style coffee culture, it is a popular spot for morning coffee, brunch, fresh juices, and casual meetups on the square.", "reviews": ["We stopped at Kavana Lattiera and really enjoyed the atmosphere. The coffee and desserts were excellent, and the place has a very nice vibe for sitting down and relaxing. One thing that stood out, though, was the wait time – we had to wait more than 30 minutes for our order, and it felt like we had been forgotten for a while. Once everything finally arrived, the quality made up for it, but the service could definitely be more attentive.", "Great place with a fresh and healthy offer! The menu is full of delicious options made from quality ingredients — from smoothie bowls and sandwiches to great breakfast choices. The açaí bowl is especially tasty and definitely worth trying. Perfect spot for a relaxed coffee or a healthy meal.", "During the vacation with my girlfriend (who only eats vegetarian and gluten free) in Croatia, we went a couple of times here. What a nice place and so many locals went there as well. The menu was only on Croatian and we had to translate but that was not a problem at all. The service, the food, everything is so nice here. And the best thing is, it’s open until 4 pm.", "Very interesting establishment set amongst apartments and shops. Inside it's a whole different feel to the outside and to what I have seen in Pula, which is very comforting and reminds me of other international cafes, and those special couple of cafes in Zagreb too. The food is so good, healthy and very thoughtful recipes. Veg will be happy. Oat milk available."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 91 462 9061", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 2.5, "description": "A popular coffee spot in Max City on Stoja, perfect for a coffee break or relaxing after shopping, with Leggiero sandwiches, Torterie Macaron desserts, a spacious terrace, and both smoking and non-smoking areas.", "reviews": ["Since my last visit to this place, I’ve noticed a more positive atmosphere, a friendlier approach, and more efficient service, which wasn’t the case in previous months. You can see the effort and the desire for improvement, and I hope they will continue at this pace and keep the quality staff who create the best impression.", "I really enjoyed coffe here. Don't know what people are talking about. The stuff isn't annoying with questions but always there if you need them. You should definitely try their macarons. But there MUST be more people on the shift. Two people (one mixing, one serving) cannot cope with two terraces and a place inside. But this is a question for the owners, not the employees..", "Besides the fact that the quality has declined over the past few years, from now on you’ll get a slice of cake for €4.10 served in a plastic container with a plastic fork. Top-notch service, no doubt! From today on, I’ll be avoiding this place."], "price": "high"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "coffee", "gallery", "cocktails", "ice_cream", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cvajner", "phone": "+385 52 216 502", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-23:00; Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.3, "description": "Art café and gallery on Pula’s main square, known for its striking historic interior, artistic atmosphere, and terrace overlooking the Forum and the Temple of Augustus.", "reviews": ["Great place to get some coffee and quick food; located right in Forum Square, so finding this place is super simple. Service could be a bit better and more organized, but otherwise everything was super tasty.", "Very nice iced coffee. Cozy enviroment, interesting design with restored paintings on the walls.", "This is in a great location if you sit outside. The Forum has a great buzz and is beautiful. Prices are quite reasonable for such a location (big draught beer €4.2) Most of the staff are busy and seem a bit a bit grumpy ( except one nice waitress) There are small menus on the tables and bills are clearly itemised. We saw a family leave after waiting ages to be served. Inside looks nice too with some old frescos. Locals here too. Worth a visit though.", "Gorgeous and cosy caffe... Well preserved historical charm done by keeping the original tapestry and blending it in with the new one. Drinks are well made and the staff is polite, very nice place to come to on a rainy day."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
4. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Ribarska Koliba", "phone": "+385 99 499 1306", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 13:00-20:00; Fr-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 13:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A refined seaside restaurant known for fresh local seafood, Mediterranean cuisine, Istrian wines, homemade desserts, and elegant dining with a sea view.", "reviews": ["A culinary highlight! The dishes are creative, refined and simply taste convincing. The service is friendly and attentive, the ambience warm and welcoming – perfect for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A little downer: The plates were cold, so the food quickly became lukewarm. Nevertheless, an all-round recommended visit!", "Exceptional food and service ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ Best lubina, stuffed swuid was excellent as well! Lovely setting for an evening meal.", "Nice view and good food! The only downside was that the main course came pretty soon after the starter. As a result, we were basically ready within an hour. We had to wait the longest for the bill 😅"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "pancakes", "waffles", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pulačinka", "phone": "+385 52 825 825", "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 14:00-22:00; We-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy dessert and pancake cafe in the center of Pula, known for sweet and savory pancakes, waffles, churros, and other treats. Guests can customize their own pancake with a wide range of spreads, toppings, fruit, biscuits, and chocolate bars, making it a popular spot for breakfast, dessert, or a casual snack.", "reviews": ["We had very tasty dessert here, a giant pancake and a wafle. Both were packed with sweet things full of calories 😀 You can select from pre-set variations of sweet or salty pancakes, or you can create your own version.", "This creperie is absolutely amazing! The pistachio sauce is the best I’ve ever had – rich, creamy, and full of flavor. On top of that, the staff are incredibly friendly and attentive, which makes the whole experience even better. Highly recommended!", "We have tried churros and custom pancake. Churros were good, but not the best that we had. But pancake was almost perfect. It was done quickly without saving on ingredients. There are many different ingredients to choose from and you can mix as much as you want. Prices are high but it is normal for Pula I guess..", "I've eaten here a palačinka with my girlfriend and it was the most Nutella I ate in a long time. Then, she had a blood sugar spike so powerful she drove 360 km without any pause. Recommended before long road trips 👍🏻"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 52 634 385", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 08:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 3.4, "description": "A modern coffee bar and snack spot in Pula City Mall, offering quality coffee, fresh juices, sandwiches, cakes and sweet treats, ideal for a relaxed coffee break while shopping.", "reviews": ["Very expensive place to drink a coffe! Really too much! A price of a coffee in a supermarket must be more cheaper than one in the centre of the city…excessively!!!", "A very relaxing place whether you sit inside or outside on the terrace, with an excellent selection of food and drinks and outstanding, dedicated staff—especially the waiter Dylan, who is very fast, helpful, friendly, and fully committed to guests at all times, regardless of the crowd and high turnover of people!", "The coffee is average, but definitely not worth €2.90. I’ve had much better coffee for less money. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only one who thinks the quality doesn’t justify the price.", "Always smiling, helpful, and quick, even when dealing with guests who can be very rude and impatient. Kudos to them for their patience—they truly make an effort and give their best to do the job as well as possible. Highly recommended!"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar AS", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "39", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A local neighborhood bar just above the Arena area in central Pula, known for a casual atmosphere, coffee, beer, and everyday drinks in a simple, social setting.", "reviews": ["A simple small one room locals bar not far from the rear of the arena. A lot nicer inside than the exterior would have you believe. Very reasonable prices. Paulicarus asked for a small Ožujsko. 2.3€ for a 0.33l bottle. Nice and cold. The 0.5l is only 30 cents more but need to drink fast to enjoy it cold. A pleasant bar for a quick beer.", "A great local bar in the back streets of Pula. I like it here away from the tourist areas 👍", "Beautiful bar, where I met new friends and the drinks are cheap. I love it!"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Giardino Bar", "phone": "+385 99 403 4680", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-24:00; Sa 07:00-01:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Giardini", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A cozy café in the center of Pula, ideal for coffee, ice cream, drinks, and a relaxing break.", "reviews": ["Nice place, great drink (teragino), the music wasn't loud, so it wasn't a problem to hear each other. And we got free chips and nuts with the drink.", "Great location and atmosphere and an extremely polite and helpful waiter, a real refreshment!", "Good music, delicious coffee, even a vegan milk option, and clean bathrooms."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Titov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "events", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central waterfront park in Pula, known for its memorial monuments, shaded walking areas, city model, and lively social atmosphere with seasonal events.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Tito's Park in Pula is a prominent public park that serves as a green oasis in the heart of the city. Named after Josip Broz Tito, the former Yugoslav leader, the park is a popular area for both locals and tourists seeking relaxation and recreation. There's also a miniature model on one side of the park.", "Nice park next to the water with many busts of famous partisans, including Tito. The main monument is also dedicated to the partisans. Worth a few pictures.", "A piece of more recent Croatian history. Has some statues, a place for kids to play, a few benches and a model of the city."]}}
3. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Sergio Endrigo", "tags": ["park", "memorial", "near_attractions", "city_center"], "description": "Small urban park in central Pula dedicated to singer-songwriter Sergio Endrigo, with commemorative installations and occasional cultural events. Today it is mostly a quiet stop with a few benches and greenery, more suitable for a short pause than as a main attraction.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "wine", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Padela", "phone": "+385 91 6085 632", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Riva", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A stylish waterfront restaurant on Pula’s Riva, specializing in handmade pasta, risotto, seafood, wine, and seasonal local ingredients.", "reviews": ["Excellent experience dining at this unique and wonderful restaurant! Beautifully decorated and very kind, professional service. We immediately felt welcomed. The waiter was also very helpful with describing the different dishes and house made pastas. Highly recommended.", "Fine dining with local touch and amazing ingredients. We were super amazed about the quality and taste of food. The pasta is perfectly cooked with carefully combined flavors and sauce. Thanks to the chef and team for the experience! 👏", "Padela is wonderful small restaurant with such a sweet atmosphere. Our server was so lovely and gave us exceptional wine recommendations. The pasta is to die for and the seafood is clearly very fresh. Highly recommend adding this place to your time in Pula!"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "neapolitan_pizza", "pasta", "italian", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Amore Pizza & Pasta", "phone": "+385 95 382 6114", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Kapitolinski trg", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A charming pizza and pasta restaurant in old town, just behind the Temple of Augustus. Known for homemade pasta, authentic Neapolitan pizza, fresh local ingredients, and a cozy atmosphere near the harbor, it is a great choice for a relaxed Italian-style meal in a historic setting.", "reviews": ["Simple, delicious, and affordable. The dough is light and crispy, tomato sauce is flavorful, and toppings are generous. We had a Margherita and a Diavola – both came out piping hot from the wood-fired oven. Service was friendly and fast. Two pizzas + two drinks cost us around €25. A solid choice if you're craving authentic pizza without tourist prices.", "At Pizzeria Amore we ordered a pizza with stracciatella and homemade pappardelle with beef. The pizza was delicious – true Neapolitan style, with a perfect crust and a rich tomato sauce. The pasta was cooked to perfection as well. However, the prices compared to portion sizes are about twice as high as what you would normally pay just across the border in Italy. Since Croatia adopted the euro, dining out has become noticeably more expensive.", "The best Neapolitan pizza in Pula. We had a big appetite for pizza and we really liked the outdoor garden behind the church of St. Augustus. We had lemon lemonade and iced tea. I chose a pizza with green pesto, mozzarella, mortadella with truffles and pistachios. Incredible taste and a great combination. I even drizzled it with chili oil and I was the happiest. My boyfriend chose a pizza with a tomato base, mozzarella, Isterian sausage and on top he had a little bit of cheese mixed with cream. Perfect choice and we really enjoyed it. Thank you very much.", "We had an amazing dinner at Amore Pizzeria! The pizza and pasta were fresh, flavorful, and beautifully presented — you can really taste the quality ingredients. The atmosphere in the Old Town courtyard was cozy and charming, and the staff were super friendly and attentive. Great wine list too! Definitely a must-visit in Pula."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["pizza", "pasta", "seafood", "desserts", "italian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Pomodoro", "phone": "+385 52 218 093", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 10:00-23:00; Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Ulica Sergijevaca", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A casual restaurant in the heart of Pula’s old town, located on one of the main central streets and serving pizza, pasta, seafood, and desserts in a lively setting.", "reviews": ["Surprisingly best restaurant we visited here. Everyday we tried some different restaurant, everything was good but this one was so good that I decided to write this review :) Waitress was very polite and helpful. Taste of food was just outstanding. This was very good experience wort every penny. We all agreed that we had to come back here. Thank you Pomodoro", "Very good pizza and tagliatelle. Waitress was very nice and helpful when we asked questions about some meals. Be careful not to order too much! Size of the meal is rather big.", "An absolutely perfect experience at Restaurant Pomodoro in Pula! 🌟 From the moment we sat down, everything was flawless – exceptional service, professional and friendly waiters who made us feel welcome right away. 🍷 The food was simply outstanding! The pizzas were a highlight – Tartufo and Quattro Formaggi were absolutely amazing, with a perfect dough that was light yet crispy in just the right way. The fish was beautifully prepared, fresh and full of flavor, a true Mediterranean delight. The white wines were perfectly chilled and paired wonderfully with the meal. 🐟🍕 Restaurant Pomodoro deserves every recommendation – a must-visit spot for a true gourmet experience in Pula! 👌✨"], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "wine", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Padela", "phone": "+385 91 6085 632", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Riva", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A stylish waterfront restaurant on Pula’s Riva, specializing in handmade pasta, risotto, seafood, wine, and seasonal local ingredients.", "reviews": ["Excellent experience dining at this unique and wonderful restaurant! Beautifully decorated and very kind, professional service. We immediately felt welcomed. The waiter was also very helpful with describing the different dishes and house made pastas. Highly recommended.", "Fine dining with local touch and amazing ingredients. We were super amazed about the quality and taste of food. The pasta is perfectly cooked with carefully combined flavors and sauce. Thanks to the chef and team for the experience! 👏", "Padela is wonderful small restaurant with such a sweet atmosphere. Our server was so lovely and gave us exceptional wine recommendations. The pasta is to die for and the seafood is clearly very fresh. Highly recommend adding this place to your time in Pula!"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Ribarska Koliba", "phone": "+385 99 499 1306", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 13:00-20:00; Fr-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 13:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A refined seaside restaurant known for fresh local seafood, Mediterranean cuisine, Istrian wines, homemade desserts, and elegant dining with a sea view.", "reviews": ["A culinary highlight! The dishes are creative, refined and simply taste convincing. The service is friendly and attentive, the ambience warm and welcoming – perfect for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A little downer: The plates were cold, so the food quickly became lukewarm. Nevertheless, an all-round recommended visit!", "Exceptional food and service ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ Best lubina, stuffed swuid was excellent as well! Lovely setting for an evening meal.", "Nice view and good food! The only downside was that the main course came pretty soon after the starter. As a result, we were basically ready within an hour. We had to wait the longest for the bill 😅"], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Verudella", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "aquarium", "military_history", "family_friendly"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress on Punta Verudela, now home to Aquarium Pula and known for its military heritage and sea-facing setting.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Ovine", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal"], "description": "Abandoned Austro-Hungarian coastal fort in the Valovine area, known for its atmospheric tunnels, overgrown walls, and striking rooftop views over the sea.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["It was a small ruin with an entrance, a hallway, some rooms and a tunnel to a small katacomb. The dark tunnel which looks like the entrance of a katacomb has a slight slope and is slippery. Unfortunately some of the rooms were used as toilets - no understanding for that... The parking lots are kind off in front of fort and very busy. So make shure to plan your visit in the morning.", "Nothing special about this place, I have only visited the exterior though. I don't know if I suggest the visit. There is a civil guard near the entrance", "A fortification overgrown in the rock. Large areas are empty and dark. For those who enjoy extreme sports, this is for you."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Verudella", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "aquarium", "military_history", "family_friendly"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress on Punta Verudela, now home to Aquarium Pula and known for its military heritage and sea-facing setting.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Kaiser Franz", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "island", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the island of Sveti Andrija in Pula, known for its circular form, layered military history, and strategic position in the middle of the harbour.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["Nice fort. It's a pity that it is neglected and completely overgrown. While sightseeing, it feels like walking through a jungle. There are a lot of snakes and rats. On the roof of the fortress there are a lot of hidden ventilation holes through which you can fall, so you need to be very careful."]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
2. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
3. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
4. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
5. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}

