2. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
3. {"type": "ruins", "properties": {"name": "ruševine Hidrobaze", "tags": ["ruins", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Former military ruin in the Hidrobaza area near Štinjan, currently in a neglected state and notable for its abandoned structure, graffiti, and position near the beach and promenade.", "rating": 3.9, "reviews": ["Interesting ruins (of an old seaplane base if I got it right) close to the beach. As usual in lost places close civilisation a lot of waste, racial slurs graffitied, and broken glass. Still quite interesting to see, but maybe don't bring your kids, don't go alone (floor partially collapsed), and watch your steps.", "I don't know who owns it at the moment, but it's an important memento of Hungarian history: a seaplane base headquarters. It's a shame.", "It's a shame these ruins have been left to decay. A wonderful 'lost place.'"]}}
