5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
2. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
4. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Stoja", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and strategic position above the southern approach to the harbour.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very beautiful places with the opportunity to jump from cliffs.", "I unexpectedly discovered this place, a mound. Fort Stoja is one of the most mysterious and 'hidden' forts in Pula. Built in 1884 by the Austro-Hungarians as part of a powerful coastal defense for the empire's main naval base. Unlike most forts, Stoja is almost completely dug into the peninsula's limestone cliff: only a massive entrance wall with a portal is visible from the outside, while the rest is hidden underground and covered by a dense pine forest. It is surrounded by a deep moat cut into the rock, once filled with water and protected by caponiers. On three sides, the fort plunges directly into the sea, making it virtually invisible from the water or from the air. Inside are long casemates, powder magazines, and posterns extending into the hillside. After the First World War, it lost its military significance and gradually became overgrown with forest, becoming a 'ghost fort.' Today the moat is dry, but the walls and entrance are impressive: it seems as if the mountain itself opens a huge door to the 19th century. An ideal place for those who enjoy the atmosphere of abandoned fortifications, peace and quiet, and views of the Adriatic without the crowds of tourists.", "Beautiful campsite, convenient for Pula by bus. The fort is not accessible and is at the top of the peninsula."]}}
5. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Paula von Preradović", "tags": ["plaque", "memorial", "historic"], "description": "Memorial plaque dedicated to Paula von Preradović, poet and author of the lyrics of the Austrian national anthem, marking the house near Pula’s Naval Park where she spent part of her childhood and youth. The plaque commemorates her literary legacy and her lasting connection to Pula.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Memorial plaque for the poet of the Austrian national anthem, who also wrote poems about Pula and lived here for some time."]}}

1. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Large hotel near the beach in Pula, offering comfortable rooms, sports and wellness facilities, and easy access to both the coast and the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 3.4, "reviews": ["It’s hard to choose a hotel based on the reviews, as everyone has an expectation. This hotel is located near the beach, in the middle of a beautiful landscape. Offers parking, wi-fi, gym, swimming pool, breakfast and others. The quaro, though old, was clean and cozy. The service from the staff was excellent, as I had made a reservation that was cancelled and I was surprised at the time, but the boy, very kind, solved the problem. Thank you very much for your attention. The price was a little above the platform, but it was already a little late and we ended up staying there.", "This place really needs some love. Sure, lots of options for breakfast, but the visual aspect of spending time here leaves much to be desired. Ancient caprets in the halls tell stories. Not ones I would like to be part of.", "It's an old hotel that must have been great in its day. Now it's worn out but makes no pretensions about itself. It has got a nice looking pool but I didn't try it. The rooms are basic and the bathroom is best described as old but functional. Generally the hotel is clean and the staff friendly."]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Hostel Art & Joy", "tags": ["hostel", "free_parking", "garden", "family_friendly"], "description": "Friendly hostel in Pula with a garden, terrace, shared kitchen, and convenient access to the Arena and other city attractions.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["We had an amazing stay in this hostel. The staff is very nice and helpful : the receptionist gave us tips on what to see and visit around the city, helped us book bikes. We were also able to change beds to be closer to each other in the room. The bedrooms and common rooms are cleaned daily and the air conditioning was appreciated. The hostel is well located, there are bus stops right next to it, it’s only a 10-minutes walk to the city center. As 2 girls travelling, we felt very confortable and safe staying at this hostel. People we met there were easygoing and we had some really nice times in the kitchen and on the terrace. To sum up : we had a wonderful vacation in Pula :) PS : the only thing that’s missing would be board games accessible to everyone.", "We had a nice stay in the private room. Everything is clean, the staff is friendly, pizzeria next door. The cute mosaique and artistic flair got us lost in long conversations about art and the meaning of life ;)", "I have stayed in Pula 5 times now. The first time was at an apartment with restricted check in times. 3pm to 5pm only. And a long walk to the centre.I was in a restaurant chatting to someone on the next table.He recommended Art and Joy hostel. I took a walk there the next day. His advice was spot on. I met the manager there and said may I have a look inside, with a possibility of staying there the following year. She agreed. Wow it was great I thought. So I booked for the next Summer. I wasn't disappointed. I have now stayed 4 times each Summer for 4 years.Close to the centre, and the staff are superb. They will help you with any issues you may have.. The hard working cleaner is great also. I recommend it. Choice of rooms to suit your requirements.And good value.. Give it a try for a few nights and then extend it if you want to. Obviously subject to availability."]}}
2. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}

