2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Battery San Giovanni", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic coastal battery above Verudela in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its ramparts, military character, and location near Aquarium Pula and the beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Very beautifully made and presented. This facility houses the second part of the aquarium, which gathers more exotic animal species and provides a look at the development and power of the Austro-Hungarian Navy. I was enchanted by everything I saw in both facilities. You should definitely visit the Pula Aquarium. It is relaxing, inspiring, enchanting. Highly recommended.", "The second part of the aquarium is located in the Baterija San Giovanni. Tickets must be purchased at the upper level. This section of the aquarium is dedicated to 'exotic' animal species and concludes with a marine exhibit. The aquariums are well worth seeing. Our children were thrilled. Important on hot days... the aquarium is air-conditioned. The conversion of the fort into an aquarium is also very well done. In short: absolutely worth seeing.", "The second part of the aquarium, with the larger animals."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
4. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Stoja", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and strategic position above the southern approach to the harbour.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very beautiful places with the opportunity to jump from cliffs.", "I unexpectedly discovered this place, a mound. Fort Stoja is one of the most mysterious and 'hidden' forts in Pula. Built in 1884 by the Austro-Hungarians as part of a powerful coastal defense for the empire's main naval base. Unlike most forts, Stoja is almost completely dug into the peninsula's limestone cliff: only a massive entrance wall with a portal is visible from the outside, while the rest is hidden underground and covered by a dense pine forest. It is surrounded by a deep moat cut into the rock, once filled with water and protected by caponiers. On three sides, the fort plunges directly into the sea, making it virtually invisible from the water or from the air. Inside are long casemates, powder magazines, and posterns extending into the hillside. After the First World War, it lost its military significance and gradually became overgrown with forest, becoming a 'ghost fort.' Today the moat is dry, but the walls and entrance are impressive: it seems as if the mountain itself opens a huge door to the 19th century. An ideal place for those who enjoy the atmosphere of abandoned fortifications, peace and quiet, and views of the Adriatic without the crowds of tourists.", "Beautiful campsite, convenient for Pula by bus. The fort is not accessible and is at the top of the peninsula."]}}
5. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}

1. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "meat", "pasta", "burgers", "beer", "wine", "cocktails", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kinema", "phone": "+385 99 164 4949", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 10:00-23:00, Fr,Sa 10:00-24:00, Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Flavijevska", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A modern pub and restaurant in Pula with a lively social atmosphere, combining great food, drinks, and entertainment in one place. Kinema is known for billiards, darts, live sports screenings, themed events, burgers, steaks, breakfast, local wines, cocktails, and craft beer, making it a popular spot for both casual hangouts and nights out with friends.", "reviews": ["Fantastic bar/restaurant. Visiting from England I was looking for somewhere to watch the Aston Villa match, walked in I believe I met the owner, said he had the game on, minute later a guy came over and said you want the Villa game on the big screen, yes I said, that’s great hospitality! The bar is extremely cool, strangely it smells wonderful in there, darts, pool all can be played. Food is excellent, we had a grazing board and chicken wings, spot on they was. Staff, really friendly and welcoming, sorry about this as I couldn’t remember her name, but Drag….. was first class.", "One of the best restaurants in Pula, especially if you’re looking for a place to eat near the Pula Arena. The food portions were huge, definitely more than enough for one person, and we left feeling very full and satisfied. The drinks were excellent and had a classy touch. The ambiance was fantastic, with great entertainment and we didn’t even realize we had stayed for over 3 hours! Highly recommended.", "What a venue! If you are looking for live sports, pool, darts or just a good atmosphere, head here. An old cinema has been transformed into a superb sports bar. A small doorway opens up to this vast multi room venue, and the screen is maaaasssssiiiiiiiivvveee. A nice welcome to fast knowledgeable service & they go to every effort to accommodate your needs. After the large main room, there's a pool room off to one side & another more intimate balcony area upstairs. The atmosphere is not too loud, so you have to shout, and the other guests are all smiling and up to banter. The menu does not do justice to the food, which was excellent. A mix of burgers, etc, to more traditional dishes Generous portios, to say the least, could not even look at the desserts menu. A real gem * kids are welcome", "This was the best restaurant I've visited in Pula. Pavle, the server was extremely pleasant and welcoming, he gave some great suggestions. I came in only to have some coffee but ended up getting the breakfast and dessert. Couldn't tell which was better. Extremely well made food, with even better staff. I couldn't recommend this place more!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Uliks", "phone": "+385 52 219 158", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg Portarata", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A historic café bar in the very center of Pula, right next to the Arch of the Sergii, known for its literary connection to James Joyce, a wide drinks selection, specialty local spirits and craft beers, and a lively atmosphere with quizzes and other events.", "reviews": ["Would highly recommend! Really nice people inside and great vibes. The decor is so cool!", "Really lovely small pub, 10/10 would recommend for a quick pint. Cool statue of James Joyce outside who used to teach English in the building back yonder.", "Best place to watch Pula‘s life, friendly service, reasonable prices, my recommendation: the Negroni", "A nice cup of coffee on a beautiful spot next to the Arch of the Sergii."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}
2. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
3. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Marie Louise", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "panoramic_view", "military_history"], "description": "Large 19th-century coastal fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its circular design and strategic views over the bay entrance.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["The remains of a large defensive fort on Musil peninsula. It was built in the 19th century and used by different armies throughout history. Today it is almost forgotten but still far from a mere ruin. The strength of its walls and beauty of its architecture are still evident. It is safe to explore, yet watch your step for scrap metal, holes and other obstacles. Just like Verudela this ruin should be restored and put to good use.", "Spectacular abandoned fort. You can explore everything. Be careful.", "There's a good, convenient entrance, but it's guarded. Closed to the curious. However, you can access the area along the western coast along a narrow path. Along the way, you'll encounter abandoned former military fortifications. It's a bit scary! Once inside, I felt like a stalker! I saw several huge peacocks. This was once a huge military base. Now everything is abandoned, but the buildings, both above and below ground, are in excellent condition."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Tegetthoff", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal", "closed_area", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Large circular Austro-Hungarian coastal fort on Veliki Brijun, preserved under military control and closed to visitors.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "wine", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Padela", "phone": "+385 91 6085 632", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Riva", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A stylish waterfront restaurant on Pula’s Riva, specializing in handmade pasta, risotto, seafood, wine, and seasonal local ingredients.", "reviews": ["Excellent experience dining at this unique and wonderful restaurant! Beautifully decorated and very kind, professional service. We immediately felt welcomed. The waiter was also very helpful with describing the different dishes and house made pastas. Highly recommended.", "Fine dining with local touch and amazing ingredients. We were super amazed about the quality and taste of food. The pasta is perfectly cooked with carefully combined flavors and sauce. Thanks to the chef and team for the experience! 👏", "Padela is wonderful small restaurant with such a sweet atmosphere. Our server was so lovely and gave us exceptional wine recommendations. The pasta is to die for and the seafood is clearly very fresh. Highly recommend adding this place to your time in Pula!"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Ribarska Koliba", "phone": "+385 99 499 1306", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Th 13:00-20:00; Fr-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 13:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A refined seaside restaurant known for fresh local seafood, Mediterranean cuisine, Istrian wines, homemade desserts, and elegant dining with a sea view.", "reviews": ["A culinary highlight! The dishes are creative, refined and simply taste convincing. The service is friendly and attentive, the ambience warm and welcoming – perfect for a relaxed lunch or dinner. A little downer: The plates were cold, so the food quickly became lukewarm. Nevertheless, an all-round recommended visit!", "Exceptional food and service ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ Best lubina, stuffed swuid was excellent as well! Lovely setting for an evening meal.", "Nice view and good food! The only downside was that the main course came pretty soon after the starter. As a result, we were basically ready within an hour. We had to wait the longest for the bill 😅"], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "pub", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bounty", "phone": "+385 52 218 088", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy Irish-style pub in city center, known for draft beer, a wide drink selection, and a comfortable terrace with a relaxed atmosphere.", "reviews": ["An excellent Irish pub with a great Irish atmosphere. Clean, tidy, good to be here As it is a bit away from the busy tourist area, it is not crowded. Guinness and local beers on tap, plus a great selection of drinks. Shaded, comfortable terrace.", "Didn't get to stay here for long (one drink) however it has a real homely feel to the place and is a really nicely situated pub. Good atmosphere and seating options, good drink choices which are more foreign options (Guinness/Heineken/Jack Daniels etc) and the prices are quite good also! Would recommend stopping in for some drinks if in the local area!", "This is a proper bar. Beautiful inside. A nice seating area outside. They have a really good selection of drinks on offer."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["italian", "croatian", "cocktails", "salads", "pizza", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Osteria Food & Wine", "phone": "+385 97 609 1198", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 11:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "38", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A cozy restaurant and wine bar near the Pula Arena, offering Roman-style pinsa, tapas-style dishes, and a wide selection of Istrian wines. Set in the shadow of the ancient amphitheater, it combines local ingredients, a relaxed atmosphere, and a warm setting that works well for both summer evenings and cozy winter dining.", "reviews": ["Very nice restaurant with terrace and beautiful interior. You can also buy ice cream there. The food was tasty and they separated pizza to two plates, which was good. The toilets are upstairs and you can have a sit there with a nice view. The bar has also many nice bottles", "Great restaurant 100 feet from the Pula Arena, the pizza is very good and the Pivo was also very good, the service was very good but it did take 30 mins for our food to come out. Our server provided us with an after meal drink at no charge for the delay.", "Everything was perfect, very unique menu and foods. Waiters are very kind and helpful.", "The food was absolutely lovely, and the service was outstanding. The waiter Adi was extremely nice and polite with a good sense of humour. We had a fantastic time. We would definitely recommend this place👌"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "MONTE ZARO", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern hostel in Pula with private bathrooms, breakfast, free parking, and a convenient location close to city attractions.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["We were here in August 2025 And it was perfect, receptionists were always nice and helpfull, the breakfast was delicious, the room was clean, new and quite nice. The location is perfect, we were 10 minutes away from the city center. So basically, i recommend this hostel to anyone, who don’t want to Pay big cash, but do want to spend time in comfort accommodation.", "Nice apartment for one night stay. Walking distance from city centre, Arena. Useful kitchen. Good value for money.", "Perfect location if you want to explore the city of Pula by foot. The room was clean and the staff was very helpful. Walls are quite thin and you can hear other people in the hall."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
5. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Stara parna lokomotiva", "tags": ["attraction", "historic", "industrial"], "description": "Historic steam locomotive displayed in Pula near the railway station, known as a preserved example of early 20th-century railway engineering and the city’s industrial heritage.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["It can be seen next to the Pula train station, is easily accessible and can be photographed."]}}

